From 24597a6d64d411fd5892932aa22ac7dc8bd8e4f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <florian.stosse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:38:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] fix the target of deprecated alias
 -e-acsl-assert-print-data

The deprecated option -e-acsl-assert-print-data was registered as an
alias of Verify_valid (-e-acsl-O-valid) instead of Print_values
(-e-acsl-O-print-values), a copy-paste slip from the -e-acsl-valid alias
just above. A command line that still uses the old option therefore
re-instrumented annotations already proven valid, and
-e-acsl-no-assert-print-data did not turn off value printing. The
deprecation warning also told users to switch to the wrong option.

Register the alias on Print_values, which is what the old option did and
what e-acsl-gcc --assert-print-data already maps to.

Test: special/e-acsl-no-assert-print-data.c gets a second run with the
deprecated -e-acsl-no-assert-print-data; its generated code is the same as
with -e-acsl-O-no-print-values (no values registered).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plugins/e-acsl/doc/Changelog                  |  4 +++
 plugins/e-acsl/src/options.ml                 |  2 +-
 .../special/e-acsl-no-assert-print-data.c     |  6 ++--
 .../e-acsl-no-assert-print-data.1.res.oracle  |  8 +++++
 .../gen_e-acsl-no-assert-print-data.1.c       | 35 +++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
